// Source: "Chaos ransomware group attribution" session (past chat)
// CRITICAL FINDING: confirmed all five DCs made outbound SMB/RPC/RDP
// connection attempts DIRECTLY to an external internet IP (216.155.157.161),
// with TCP handshakes completing before a firewall elsewhere tore the
// sessions down. This confirms ZERO egress/outbound filtering between the
// DCs and the open internet on these ports — distinct from, and arguably
// worse than, "the host firewall was disabled." A DC should never reach a
// public IP on these ports under any circumstance. The session teardown
// observed elsewhere in the stack was a lucky, incidental catch — not a
// designed control. This belongs in the Security Review as its own gap,
// distinct from the firewall-disabled finding, elevated to CRITICAL.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(90d)
| where DeviceName has_any ("hqdc01","hqdc02","hqdc03","opclddc01","opclddc02")
| where RemotePort in (445, 135, 3389, 5985, 5986)
| where not(ipv4_is_private(RemoteIP))
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, RemoteIP, RemotePort, InitiatingProcessFileName
| order by Timestamp asc
